--
User-reported: out-of-class definition of a member of a member class
template of a class template, two-level template header
  template <typename T, uint8_t N, bool W> template <bool E>
  void Outer<T, N, W>::reference<E>::on_write() { ... }
Two defects: the parser treated `reference<` after the dependent
qualifier `Outer<T, N, W>::` as less-than (N5008 [temp.dep.type]/1,5 +
[temp.names]/3: a member of the current instantiation needs no
`template` keyword; decided by a tentative `<...>` parse followed by
`::`), and the typechecker's class-template-member path dropped the
7-component shape, leaving the member bodiless ([temp.mem]/1: the
definition is grafted onto the member's in-class declaration).
